    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1667396292524",
     "position": 1,
     "url": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1667396292524",
     "name": "How do you thicken chicken and dumplings?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "With this recipe, I add flour to each dumpling and it helps to thicken it up. You can also make a slurry by whisking 3 tablespoons of cornstarch with 3 tablespoons of water and stir that into the pot. Bring the mixture to a boil or set it on high and it will thicken.",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1622855426131",
     "position": 2,
     "url": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1622855426131",
     "name": "Can I use fresh chicken breasts instead of frozen?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Absolutely! I used frozen chicken breasts (which are much cheaper than their fresh counterparts - but still just as yummy!) The time might need to be adjusted slightly for fresh chicken breasts. You can also use different cuts like chicken thighs.",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1622855625459",
     "position": 3,
     "url": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1622855625459",
     "name": "Do I need to use a specific brand of biscuits?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "I like the Pillsbury Grands biscuits but you can use any of your favorite refrigerated biscuits.",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1622857443431",
     "position": 4,
     "url": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1622857443431",
     "name": "Why roll the biscuit dough in flour?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "This helps to thicken up the chicken broth. It also helps to keep the dumplings from sticking together. ",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1667396394859",
     "position": 5,
     "url": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1667396394859",
     "name": "What goes along with chicken and dumplings as a side?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "We like to serve these with some vegetables. Generally, steamed broccoli, <a href=\"https://www.thecountrycook.net/maple-glazed-carrots/\">carrots</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.thecountrycook.net/bacon-garlic-green-beans/\">green beans</a>. ",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1667396578943",
     "position": 6,
     "url": "https://www.thecountrycook.net/crock-pot-chicken-and-dumplings/#faq-question-1667396578943",
     "name": "How long do dumplings take in the slow cooker?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Once you add the dumplings to the crock pot, it will take 1 to 1-1/2 hours to cook.",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
